<%# Shot from a real camera by tools/webui-gallery; run it again when the WebUI
    changes shape. The list of screens, and the captions, come from
    config/webui_gallery.yml so that the tool and this page cannot disagree
    about what the gallery contains.

    The two pages with a live player show a beach rather than the bench of
    cables the lab camera actually faces -- see the credit under the grid. The
    scene is laid over the <video> in the DOM at capture time, the same way the
    lab's address and MAC are rewritten out of the text.

    Two files per screenshot. The tile loads the 1200px one, and the zoom modal
    swaps in the 2560px original from data-zoom -- both are 2x for the size they
    are shown at, because a 1x capture is what made the old gallery look soft on
    every Retina display. %>
<article class="webinterface">
  <header>
    <h2><%= t('.title') %></h2>
  </header>

  <p class="lead col-lg-8"><%= t('.intro') %></p>

  <div id="screens" class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-xl-3 g-3">
    <% WebuiGallery.screens.each do |screen| %>
      <div class="col">
        <figure class="mb-0">
          <%= image_tag screen.tile,
                        class: 'border img-fluid img-zoom',
                        alt: screen.alt,
                        loading: 'lazy', decoding: 'async',
                        data: { zoom: image_path(screen.full) } %>
          <figcaption class="small text-muted mt-1"><%= screen.caption %></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <p class="small text-muted mt-3 col-lg-8"><%= t('.scene_credit_html') %></p>
</article>

<%= render 'pages/zoom' %>
